<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $29.34 bln on June 27.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $29.34 bln on June 27.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $29.34 billion on June 27 from $28.83 billion on June 20, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Saturday.  </p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  June 27     June 20	June 28</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     25,387	24,876	17,527</p>
<p>    Gold				 3,954	 3,954	 4,509</p>
<p>    SDRs				     3	     3	   127</p>
<p>    Total			     29,344	28,833	22,163</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
